contentText:
Kelly Clarkson just signed off of The Kelly Clarkson Show for the last time, ending her Daytime Emmy-winning talk show after seven seasons with an emotional episode that featured her two children, River and Remington.

The singer&#8217;s son and daughter joined their superstar mom for the final installment, which aired Monday (Aug. 31) and featured a special Kellyoke performance of &#8220;Golden&#8221; from KPop Demon Hunters . And after seven years covering other artists&#8217; songs for the segment, Clarkson performed a couple of her own: &#8220;Since U Been Gone&#8221; and &#8220;Stronger.&#8221;

